# Courtside environment variables
#
# Copy to .env.local for local development (.env* is gitignored), and set the
# same key in Vercel: Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# NOTE: VITE_* values are inlined into the public client bundle at build time.
# Never put a secret here. A Google OAuth *Client ID* is not a secret — it is
# visible in the OAuth request, and access is restricted by the "Authorized
# JavaScript origins" list in Google Cloud Console. (The GIS token flow this
# app uses has no client secret at all.)
#
# Setting this means cloud sync works on any device with no copy-paste, and
# survives clearing site data. A per-device override is still available in
# Settings → Cloud sync.

VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=1234567890-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com
